{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The rewrite lemma concerns a component of a vector-valued time derivative, while the goal contains the time derivative of a scalar component. Establishing their equality first via the derivative-of-application simp rule makes the existing rewrite applicable.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  have hMax := (isExtrema_iff_gauss_ampere_magneticFieldMatrix hA J hJ).mp h\\n  have hGauss :\\n      (fun y => ∑ j, ∂[j] (A.electricField 𝓕.c t · j) y) =\\n        fun y => J.chargeDensity 𝓕.c t y / 𝓕.ε₀ := by\\n    funext y\\n    exact (hMax t y).1\\n  have hDerivApply : ∀ s,\\n      ∂ₜ (A.electricField 𝓕.c · x i) s =\\n        (∂ₜ (A.electricField 𝓕.c · x)) s i := by\\n    intro s\\n    simp (disch := fun_prop)\\n  conv_lhs =>\\n    enter [1, s]\\n    rw [hDerivApply s]\\n    rw [time_deriv_electricField_of_isExtrema hA J hJ h]\\n  simp (disch := fun_prop)\\n  simp_rw [time_deriv_magneticFieldMatrix A (hA.of_le (right_eq_inf.mp rfl))]\\n  simp (disch := fun_prop)\\n  simp only [Finset.sum_sub_distrib]\\n  conv_lhs =>\\n    enter [1, 2, j, 2]\\n    rw [Space.deriv_commute _\\n      (electricField_space_contDiff _ (hA.of_le (right_eq_inf.mp rfl)) t j)]\\n  rw [← Space.deriv_fun_sum]\\n  rw [hGauss]\\n  simp (disch := fun_prop)\\n  simp only [FreeSpace.c_sq]\\n  field_simp\\n  ring\"}"}}
